# Undergraduate Electrical Engineering Curricular Architecture
#
# ABET-accredited Bachelor of Science (B.S.) in Electrical Engineering: circuits, signals and systems, analog electronics, electromagnetics, and power.

#>spw_cache_univ_undergrad_ee
#:cache #!electrical_engineering
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Model the four-year undergraduate curriculum for an ABET-accredited Bachelor of Science in Electrical Engineering, articulating circuit analysis, signal transforms, analog microelectronics, and electromagnetics."
  ~#accreditation: "ABET EAC Criteria for Electrical, Electronics, and Communication Engineering"
}

^["linear_circuit_analysis_and_ac_networks"]{
  sophomore_gateway: "Circuits I & II with Circuit Prototyping Laboratory."
  circuit_foundations: #[
    "Kirchhoff's Laws & Network Theorems: KCL, KVL, nodal and mesh analysis, Thevenin/Norton equivalents, and maximum power transfer",
    "Operational Amplifier Circuits: Ideal op-amp golden rules, inverting/non-inverting configurations, instrumentation amplifiers, and active filters",
    "Transient Dynamics: First-order RC/RL step response, second-order RLC differential equations, damping ratio zeta, and resonant ringing",
    "Sinusoidal Steady-State: Phasor transform, complex impedance Z, admittance Y, AC real/reactive/apparent power, and power factor correction",
    "Frequency Resonance: Series and parallel RLC resonant tanks, quality factor Q, and 3dB bandwidth calculations"
  ]
}

^["signals_linear_systems_and_transforms"]{
  sophomore_junior_core: "Continuous and Discrete Signals and Systems."
  signal_disciplines: .{
    time_domain_foundations: #[
      "Classification: Continuous-Time (CT) vs Discrete-Time (DT), energy vs power signals, and causality/stability conditions",
      "Convolution: Impulse response h(t), LTI system response via convolution integral and discrete convolution sum"
    ]
    frequency_domain_transforms: #[
      "Fourier Analysis: Continuous Fourier Series (harmonic decomposition), CTFT, DTFT, and Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) computational mechanics",
      "Laplace Transform: Bilateral/unilateral Laplace, Region of Convergence (ROC), transfer function H(s), pole-zero constellation, and BIBO stability",
      "Z-Transform: Discrete system transfer functions H(z), unit circle stability, and digital FIR/IIR filter synthesis",
      "Sampling Theorem: Nyquist-Shannon sampling rate (fs >= 2*B), spectral aliasing, and anti-aliasing reconstruction filters"
    ]
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["semiconductor_devices_and_analog_electronics"]{
  junior_core: "Electronic Circuits and Semiconductor Physics Lab."
  microelectronics: #[
    "p-n Junction Diodes: Built-in potential, depletion width, drift/diffusion currents, Shockley diode equation, and Zener reverse breakdown",
    "MOSFET Device Physics: Inversion layer formation, threshold voltage Vth, triode and saturation regimes, square-law model, and channel-length modulation lambda",
    "Bipolar Junction Transistors (BJT): Forward-active, saturation, and cutoff operations; Ebers-Moll and hybrid-pi small-signal models",
    "Single & Multi-Stage Amplifiers: Common-source, common-drain, and common-gate topologies; differential amplifier pairs and active current mirrors",
    "Frequency Response & Feedback: High-frequency parasitic capacitances, Miller multiplication theorem, negative feedback topologies, and Bode stability margins"
  ]
}

^["electromagnetics_and_wave_transmission"]{
  junior_core: "Electromagnetic Fields, Waves, and Transmission Lines."
  wave_physics: .{
    maxwell_field_equations: "Differential and integral Maxwell equations, Lorentz gauge, plane waves in lossless/lossy media, skin depth, and Poynting vector flux"
    transmission_lines: #[
      "Distributed circuit model (R, L, G, C parameters), telegrapher's equations, and characteristic impedance Z0",
      "Voltage Standing Wave Ratio (VSWR), reflection coefficient Gamma, and bounce diagrams for transient digital pulses",
      "Smith Chart: Graphical impedance matching using single-stub and quarter-wavelength transmission line transformers",
      "Waveguides & Antennas: Rectangular metallic waveguides (TE/TM modes, cutoff frequencies) and dipole radiation patterns"
    ]
  }[reg=facet]
}

^["power_systems_and_electromechanical_energy"]{
  senior_core: "Energy Conversion and Power Systems."
  power_engineering: #[
    "Three-Phase AC Networks: Balanced Y and Delta generator/load configurations, per-phase equivalent circuits, and line-to-line vs line-to-neutral voltages",
    "Power Transformers: Magnetic core hysteresis, leakage inductance, ideal transformer scaling, and per-unit normalization",
    "Electric Machinery: Three-phase induction motors (torque-slip curves, rotor equivalent circuit), synchronous generators, and brushless DC motors",
    "Power Electronics: Switched-mode power supplies, buck/boost DC-DC converters, pulse-width modulation (PWM) inverters, and grid interconnects"
  ]
}

^["taste"]{
  ~#taste: "Undergraduate electrical engineering is the art of giving invisible electromagnetic fields an architecture that performs work and carries thought."
  ~#wonder: "Why does the Laplace s-plane transform a horrifying system of coupled high-order differential equations into simple high-school algebra?"

  principles: #[
    "Impedance matching is everywhere: From microwave transmission lines to audio amplifiers, maximum power transfers only when source and load impedances match.",
    "Ground is not a magical sink: Current flows only in closed loops; always trace where the return current travels on the circuit board.",
    "Noise is physics, not bad luck: Johnson-Nyquist thermal noise and shot noise set absolute physical limits on the smallest signal you can detect."
  ]
}

^"invariants"{
  "Analog circuit designs must demonstrate phase margins greater than 45 degrees to guarantee feedback loop stability.",
  "Digital transmission line traces must be terminated with characteristic impedance when signal rise time is less than twice the propagation delay.",
  "High-voltage laboratory experiments require dual-operator presence and verified physical grounding rods before contact.",
}

#>wonder_undergrad_ee_1
?["How does the physical fabrication of custom microwave microstrip filters on FR-4 boards alter student understanding of Maxwell's boundary conditions?"]{
  #:depth #!pedagogical ~#lens(rf_hardware_intuition)
  ~#hypothesis: "Students who lay out, mill, and test microstrip bandpass filters with a vector network analyzer (VNA) identify parasitic coupling and dielectric dispersion 50% faster than those using 2D circuit simulators alone."
  !probe{ "Measure filter design iteration counts and insertion loss prediction accuracy across physical RF prototyping vs simulation-only student cohorts." }
  $%[rf.s21_insertion_loss_accuracy_db, pedagogy.vna_troubleshooting_proficiency]
}
